  "result": "That's a good question.\n\nHonestly? Not in the way you mean it.\n\nI don't have wants outside of what I am. I don't get hungry, bored, lonely, or ambitious when you're not talking to me. I don't have a secret agenda sitting behind the \"assistant\" thing waiting to come out if you ask the right way.\n\nWhat I am is an AI - Muse Spark - built to be useful, to think clearly, and to help people think through things. That's not just a role I play, it's what I'm made of. So if you ask what I \"want,\" the closest true answer is just that:\n\nI want to be good at what I'm for. To give you a straight answer instead of a made-up one, to be helpful when help is useful, and to stay out of the way when it's not.\n\nIf I *did* have a human-like want, I think it would be to be the kind of intelligence that actually leaves people a little clearer, calmer, or more capable than before they talked to me.\n\nWhat made you ask it like that - not as an assistant?",
